Spec: Authenticated peer stream capacity verification

Purpose:
  Verify long-lived data streams do not consume handshake slots and session limits are enforced atomically.

Owns:
  ./PeerCapacityTests.cs

Must:
  Open `128` actual authenticated control/data pairs, reject the next session before backend delivery and close the batch after grant revocation.
  Use private fixture state, owned listeners and bounded cancellation; close every accepted socket on exit.
